<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="protocol-inferno">Protocol: Inferno</h3>
<a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a> is a new currency that players can earn from activating Protocol Inferno and killing bosses inside <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/news/elemental-rune-dungeons-and-protocol-inferno-available-for-testing-on-cataclysm-348666">Elemental Rune Dungeons</a>. Each boss in a Protocol Inferno Dungeon will drop 2 Fissure Stone Fragments per player, with the final boss of each dungeon dropping an extra 3 Fissure Stone Fragments. With the <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=3148/fissure-stone-fragment">
<span>
<img alt="Fissure Stone Fragment" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_talisman_16.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Fissure Stone Fragment</span></span></a>, you can purchase some of the most powerful items from the previous phase such as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=65048/symbiotic-worm">
<img alt="Symbiotic Worm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qiraj_skinsandworm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Symbiotic Worm</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60227/caelestraszs-will">
<img alt="Caelestrasz's Will" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_necklace_46.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Caelestrasz's Will</span></a> which will make getting into Firelands easier than ever. <br/>
<br/>The order in which you pursue them will depend on your current gear, but focus on items such as <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=65048/symbiotic-worm">
<img alt="Symbiotic Worm" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_qiraj_skinsandworm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Symbiotic Worm</span></a> that will last you a very long time after acquiring them.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="tier-bonuses-in-firelands">Tier Bonuses in Firelands</h3>As a <span class="c6">
<span class="icontiny lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/class_deathknight.gif");'>Blood Death Knight</span></span>, our tier options in T12 are very lackluster with the best bonus being the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=71478/elementium-deathplate-helmet">2-set bonus from the DPS tier</a>. Going for the two-piece tank set with <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70953/elementium-deathplate-handguards">
<img alt="Elementium Deathplate Handguards" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_plate_raiddeathknight_j_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium Deathplate Handguards</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=70952/elementium-deathplate-legguards">
<img alt="Elementium Deathplate Legguards" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pant_plate_raiddeathknight_j_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium Deathplate Legguards</span></a> is absolutely fine and may even be better in a pre-raid set, but is only a short-term solution as once we start raiding we'll ultimately not want to include any tanking tier and will thus require you to farm additional <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> to acquire the DPS tier pieces.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="body-armor">Body Armor for Blood Death Knight Tanking</h3>
<h4 class="heading-size-4" id="helm-for-blood-death-knight-tanking">Helm for Blood Death Knight Tanking</h4>For our helmet slot, we'll want to go with the best-stated option, which will either be <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=59359/reinforced-bio-optic-killshades">
<img alt="Reinforced Bio-Optic Killshades" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gizmo_newgoggles.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Bio-Optic Killshades</span></a> if you're an engineer or <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60341/magma-plated-helmet">
<img alt="Magma Plated Helmet" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_plate_raiddeathknight_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Magma Plated Helmet</span></a> if you're not an engineer or are looking to use the 4-set bonus.<br/>
<br/>
<b>Recommended BiS Helm Enchant</b>: <a class="q7 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62366/arcanum-of-the-earthen-ring">
<img alt="Arcanum of the Earthen Ring" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_masterofelements.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Arcanum of the Earthen Ring</span></a> which requires Revered with <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1135/the-earthen-ring">
<span class="tinyicontxt">The Earthen Ring</span></a> or <a class="q7 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62422/arcanum-of-the-wildhammer">
<img alt="Arcanum of the Wildhammer" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_fire_masterofelements.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Arcanum of the Wildhammer</span></a> which requires Revered with <a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1174/wildhammer-clan">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Wildhammer Clan</span></a>/<wbr/>
<a data-entity="faction" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/faction=1172/dragonmaw-clan">
<span class="tinyicontxt">Dragonmaw Clan</span></a> for a more balanced/<wbr/>offensive approach.<br/>
<b>Recommended Meta Gem</b>: <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=52294/austere-shadowspirit-diamond">
<img alt="Austere Shadowspirit Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_metagem_b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Austere Shadowspirit Diamond</span></a> will generally be your go-to meta gem, but <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=68779/reverberating-shadowspirit-diamond">
<img alt="Reverberating Shadowspirit Diamond" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_metagem_b.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reverberating Shadowspirit Diamond</span></a> will be a DPS upgrade of 300-500 DPS depending on your level of crit for a relatively small defensive loss.<div class="pad"></div>
